<!-- 9 -->
<section class="sec" id="sec-secondary">
  <div class="sec-h"><span class="sec-n">09</span><h2>Secondary Compression</h2></div>

  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="vcard v-vio">
      <span class="vtag">Secondary settlement</span>
      <div class="eq">\[ S_s = C'_\alpha H \log\frac&#123;t_2&#125;&#123;t_1&#125;, \qquad C'_\alpha = \frac&#123;C_\alpha&#125;&#123;1+e_p&#125; \]</div>
      <p class="small">t<sub>1</sub> is the time at which primary consolidation ends; e<sub>p</sub> is the void ratio at that moment.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="vcard v-blu">
      <span class="vtag">When to worry</span>
      <p>Negligible in most inorganic clays &mdash; often under 10% of primary. But in <strong>peat and organic soils</strong> it can exceed the primary settlement entirely and continue for decades. Note it is logarithmic in time: each additional log cycle adds the same increment, so it never quite stops.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 10 -->
<section class="sec" id="sec-examples">
  <div class="sec-h"><span class="sec-n">10</span><h2>Worked Examples</h2></div>

  <div class="example">
    <div class="ex-h"><span>Example 1</span><h4>Normally Consolidated Clay</h4></div>
    <p class="prob"><strong>Problem:</strong> A 4 m clay layer has e&#8320; = 0.90, C<sub>c</sub> = 0.32, and &sigma;'&#8320; = 110 kPa at mid-depth. The clay is normally consolidated. A new foundation raises the stress at mid-depth by &Delta;&sigma;' = 50 kPa. Find the primary consolidation settlement.</p>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><b>1</b><div>NC, so &sigma;'<sub>c</sub> = &sigma;'&#8320; = 110 kPa and the whole increment is on the virgin line.</div></div>
      <div class="step"><b>2</b><div>\( \dfrac&#123;C_c H&#125;&#123;1+e_0&#125; = \dfrac&#123;0.32(4)&#125;&#123;1.90&#125; = 0.6737\text&#123;m&#125; \)</div></div>
      <div class="step"><b>3</b><div>\( \log\dfrac&#123;110+50&#125;&#123;110&#125; = \log 1.4545 = 0.1627 \)</div></div>
      <div class="step"><b>4</b><div>\( S_c = 0.6737 \times 0.1627 = 0.1096\text&#123;m&#125; \)</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ans"><strong>Answer:</strong> S<sub>c</sub> = 110 mm.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="example">
    <div class="ex-h"><span>Example 2</span><h4>The Same Clay, Overconsolidated</h4></div>
    <p class="prob"><strong>Problem:</strong> Identical layer and identical load, but the clay is overconsolidated with &sigma;'<sub>c</sub> = 190 kPa and C<sub>s</sub> = 0.06. Find the settlement.</p>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><b>1</b><div><strong>Check the case:</strong> \( \sigma'_0 + \Delta\sigma' = 160\text&#123;kPa&#125; &lt; \sigma'_c = 190\text&#123;kPa&#125; \) &mdash; the load never reaches the preconsolidation pressure, so this is Case 2, entirely on the recompression line.</div></div>
      <div class="step"><b>2</b><div>\( \dfrac&#123;C_s H&#125;&#123;1+e_0&#125; = \dfrac&#123;0.06(4)&#125;&#123;1.90&#125; = 0.1263\text&#123;m&#125; \)</div></div>
      <div class="step"><b>3</b><div>\( S_c = 0.1263 \times 0.1627 = 0.0206\text&#123;m&#125; \)</div></div>
      <div class="step"><b>4</b><div><strong>Now push harder:</strong> if instead &Delta;&sigma;' = 120 kPa, then &sigma;'&#8320;+&Delta;&sigma;' = 230 &gt; 190, so Case 3 applies: \( S_c = 0.1263\log\frac&#123;190&#125;&#123;110&#125; + 0.6737\log\frac&#123;230&#125;&#123;190&#125; = 0.030 + 0.056 = 0.086\text&#123;m&#125; \)</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ans"><strong>Answer:</strong> 21 mm &mdash; against 110 mm for the same load on the same clay when normally consolidated, a factor of 5. Push past &sigma;'<sub>c</sub> (step 4) and settlement jumps to 86 mm, because the second half of the load rides the steep virgin line.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="example">
    <div class="ex-h"><span>Example 3</span><h4>How Long Will It Take?</h4></div>
    <p class="prob"><strong>Problem:</strong> The 4 m clay layer of Example 1 is sandwiched between sand above and below, with c<sub>v</sub> = 2.5 m&sup2;/year. Find the time for 50% and 90% consolidation, and the settlement at each.</p>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><b>1</b><div><strong>Drainage path:</strong> sand on both faces, so \( H_&#123;dr&#125; = H/2 = 2.0\text&#123;m&#125; \)</div></div>
      <div class="step"><b>2</b><div><strong>U = 50% (&lt; 60%):</strong> \( T_v = \frac&#123;\pi&#125;&#123;4&#125;(0.50)^2 = 0.1963 \), so \( t = \dfrac&#123;T_v H_&#123;dr&#125;^2&#125;&#123;c_v&#125; = \dfrac&#123;0.1963(2.0)^2&#125;&#123;2.5&#125; = 0.31\text&#123;yr&#125; \) (about 3.8 months)</div></div>
      <div class="step"><b>3</b><div><strong>U = 90% (&gt; 60%):</strong> \( T_v = 1.781 - 0.933\log(10) = 0.848 \), so \( t = \dfrac&#123;0.848(4)&#125;&#123;2.5&#125; = 1.36\text&#123;yr&#125; \)</div></div>
      <div class="step"><b>4</b><div><strong>Settlements:</strong> 50% of 110 mm = 55 mm; 90% of 110 mm = 99 mm.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ans"><strong>Answer:</strong> 50% (55 mm) in 0.31 yr; 90% (99 mm) in 1.36 yr. Note the last 40% takes four times as long as the first 50% &mdash; consolidation has a very long tail. If drainage were single-sided, H<sub>dr</sub> would double and every time would be <strong>four times</strong> longer.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 11 -->
<section class="sec" id="sec-quiz">
  <div class="sec-h"><span class="sec-n">11</span><h2>Quick Reference &amp; Quick Check</h2></div>

  <div class="qref">
    <div><span>Total settlement</span><span>S<sub>t</sub> = S<sub>e</sub> + S<sub>c</sub> + S<sub>s</sub></span></div>
    <div><span>Elastic settlement</span><span>S<sub>e</sub> = q<sub>o</sub>B(1&minus;&mu;&sup2;)I<sub>s</sub>I<sub>f</sub>/E<sub>s</sub></span></div>
    <div><span>OCR</span><span>&sigma;'<sub>c</sub> / &sigma;'&#8320;</span></div>
    <div><span>NC settlement</span><span>(C<sub>c</sub>H/(1+e&#8320;))log[(&sigma;'&#8320;+&Delta;&sigma;')/&sigma;'&#8320;]</span></div>
    <div><span>OC below &sigma;'<sub>c</sub></span><span>use C<sub>s</sub> in place of C<sub>c</sub></span></div>
    <div><span>Time factor</span><span>T<sub>v</sub> = c<sub>v</sub>t/H<sub>dr</sub>&sup2;</span></div>
    <div><span>Drainage path</span><span>H/2 double-drained, H single</span></div>
    <div><span>T<sub>v</sub> at U=50% / 90%</span><span>0.197 / 0.848</span></div>
    <div><span>Secondary</span><span>S<sub>s</sub> = C'<sub>&alpha;</sub>H log(t&#8322;/t&#8321;)</span></div>
    <div><span>Typical C<sub>s</sub>/C<sub>c</sub></span><span>1/5 to 1/10</span></div>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" id="quiz">
    <div class="q" data-a="1">
      <p>1. A building settles 80 mm uniformly across its whole footprint. Another settles 25 mm at one corner and 5 mm at the other. Which is more likely to be damaged?</p>
      <button data-v="0">The first &mdash; it settled far more in total</button>
      <button data-v="1">The second &mdash; differential settlement, not total, is what cracks structures</button>
      <button data-v="2">Neither; both are within normal limits</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q" data-a="2">
      <p>2. Why is consolidation settlement slow while elastic settlement is immediate?</p>
      <button data-v="0">Clay is stiffer than sand</button>
      <button data-v="1">The load is applied gradually during construction</button>
      <button data-v="2">Consolidation requires pore water to physically drain out of the soil</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q" data-a="0">
      <p>3. A clay has OCR = 3. A modest load is applied that keeps &sigma;'&#8320;+&Delta;&sigma;' below &sigma;'<sub>c</sub>. Compared with the same clay normally consolidated, settlement will be:</p>
      <button data-v="0">Much smaller &mdash; it stays on the flat recompression line (C<sub>s</sub>)</button>
      <button data-v="1">About the same &mdash; OCR does not affect settlement</button>
      <button data-v="2">Much larger &mdash; overconsolidated clay is more compressible</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q" data-a="2">
      <p>4. A clay layer drained on both faces reaches 90% consolidation in 2 years. If the lower sand layer were absent (single drainage), how long would it take?</p>
      <button data-v="0">2 years &mdash; unchanged</button>
      <button data-v="1">4 years &mdash; twice as long</button>
      <button data-v="2">8 years &mdash; the drainage path doubles and time goes as its square</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div id="quiz-score" class="quiz-score"></div>
</section>

<footer class="chapter-nav">
  <a href="/civil/cee340/slope-stability">&larr; Ch. 11: Slope Stability</a>
  <a href="/civil/cee340/soil-investigation">Next: Soil Investigation &rarr;</a>
</footer>

<script is:inline>
(function(){
  const g=id=>document.getElementById(id), v=id=>+g(id).value;
  const L=Math.log10;

  function settle(){
    const H=v('st-h'), e0=v('st-e0'), Cc=v('st-cc'), Cs=v('st-cs');
    const s0=v('st-s0'), sc=Math.max(v('st-sc'), v('st-s0')), ds=v('st-ds');
    if(H<=0||e0<=-1||s0<=0||ds<0){ g('st-res').innerHTML='<div class="verdict v-fail"><span>Check inputs</span></div>'; return; }
    const sf=s0+ds, mc=Cc*H/(1+e0), ms=Cs*H/(1+e0);
    let S, kase, detail;
    if (Math.abs(sc-s0) < 1e-9){
      kase='Case 1 — normally consolidated'; S=mc*L(sf/s0);
      detail=`<div class="res"><span>Virgin line only</span><b>C<sub>c</sub> = ${Cc}</b></div>`;
    } else if (sf <= sc){
      kase='Case 2 — OC, stays below σ\'c'; S=ms*L(sf/s0);
      detail=`<div class="res"><span>Recompression only</span><b>C<sub>s</sub> = ${Cs}</b></div>`;
    } else {
      kase='Case 3 — OC, crosses σ\'c';
      const p1=ms*L(sc/s0), p2=mc*L(sf/sc); S=p1+p2;
      detail=`<div class="res"><span>Recompression part</span><b>${(p1*1000).toFixed(1)} mm</b></div>`+
             `<div class="res"><span>Virgin part</span><b>${(p2*1000).toFixed(1)} mm</b></div>`;
    }
    const ocr=sc/s0;
    g('st-res').innerHTML =
      `<div class="${sf<=sc&&ocr>1?'verdict v-pass':'res'}"><span>${kase}</span><b>OCR ${ocr.toFixed(2)}</b></div>`+
      `<div class="res"><span>&sigma;'&#8320; &rarr; &sigma;'<sub>f</sub></span><b>${s0} &rarr; ${sf.toFixed(0)} kPa</b></div>`+
      detail+
      `<div class="res"><span>Primary settlement S<sub>c</sub></span><b>${(S*1000).toFixed(1)} mm</b></div>`;

    // e–log σ' figure
    const W=300,Hh=170,x0=42,y0=140,xr=245,yr=105;
    const lo=L(Math.max(1,s0*0.45)), hi=L(Math.max(sf,sc)*2.1), span=hi-lo||1;
    const PX=s=>x0+(L(s)-lo)/span*xr;
    const eAt=s=> s<=sc ? e0-Cs*(L(s)-L(s0)) : e0-Cs*(L(sc)-L(s0))-Cc*(L(s)-L(sc));
    const emin=eAt(Math.max(sf,sc)*2.0), emax=e0+0.04;
    const PY=e=>y0-(e-emin)/((emax-emin)||1)*yr;
    const seg=(a,b,col)=>`<line x1="${PX(a).toFixed(1)}" y1="${PY(eAt(a)).toFixed(1)}" x2="${PX(b).toFixed(1)}" y2="${PY(eAt(b)).toFixed(1)}" stroke="${col}" stroke-width="2"/>`;
    let curve = seg(Math.max(1,s0*0.5), sc, 'var(--teal)');
    if (Math.max(sf,sc)*2 > sc) curve += seg(sc, Math.max(sf,sc)*2, 'var(--amb)');
    g('st-fig').innerHTML=`
    <svg viewBox="0 0 ${W} ${Hh}" style="width:100%;height:auto">
      <line x1="${x0}" y1="${y0-yr-8}" x2="${x0}" y2="${y0}" stroke="var(--bdr2)"/>
      <line x1="${x0}" y1="${y0}" x2="${x0+xr+8}" y2="${y0}" stroke="var(--bdr2)"/>
      ${curve}
      <line x1="${PX(s0).toFixed(1)}" y1="${y0}" x2="${PX(s0).toFixed(1)}" y2="${PY(eAt(s0)).toFixed(1)}" stroke="var(--txt2)" stroke-width=".8" stroke-dasharray="3,2"/>
      <line x1="${PX(sf).toFixed(1)}" y1="${y0}" x2="${PX(sf).toFixed(1)}" y2="${PY(eAt(sf)).toFixed(1)}" stroke="var(--rust)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3,2"/>
      ${sc>s0?`<line x1="${PX(sc).toFixed(1)}" y1="${y0}" x2="${PX(sc).toFixed(1)}" y2="${PY(eAt(sc)).toFixed(1)}" stroke="var(--amb)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2,2"/><text x="${PX(sc).toFixed(1)}" y="${y0+11}" font-size="8" fill="var(--amb)" text-anchor="middle">σ'c</text>`:''}
      <circle cx="${PX(s0).toFixed(1)}" cy="${PY(eAt(s0)).toFixed(1)}" r="3" fill="var(--txt2)"/>
      <circle cx="${PX(sf).toFixed(1)}" cy="${PY(eAt(sf)).toFixed(1)}" r="3" fill="var(--rust)"/>
      <text x="${PX(s0).toFixed(1)}" y="${y0+11}" font-size="8" fill="var(--txt2)" text-anchor="middle">σ'₀</text>
      <text x="${PX(sf).toFixed(1)}" y="${y0-6}" font-size="8" fill="var(--rust)" text-anchor="middle">σ'f</text>
      <text x="16" y="${y0-yr/2}" font-size="8.5" fill="var(--txt2)" transform="rotate(-90 16 ${y0-yr/2})" text-anchor="middle">void ratio e</text>
      <text x="${x0+xr/2}" y="${Hh-4}" font-size="8.5" fill="var(--txt2)" text-anchor="middle">log σ' (kPa)</text>
    </svg>`;
  }
  ['st-h','st-e0','st-cc','st-cs','st-s0','st-sc','st-ds'].forEach(id=>g(id).addEventListener('input',settle));
  settle();

  function TvOf(U){ return U<60 ? Math.PI/4*Math.pow(U/100,2) : 1.781-0.933*L(100-U); }

  function timeRate(){
    const H=v('tr-h'), div=+g('tr-drain').value, cv=v('tr-cv'), Sc=v('tr-sc'), U=v('tr-u');
    g('tr-u-v').textContent=U;
    if(H<=0||cv<=0){ g('tr-res').innerHTML='<div class="verdict v-fail"><span>Check inputs</span></div>'; return; }
    const Hdr=H/div, Tv=TvOf(U), t=Tv*Hdr*Hdr/cv;
    const months=t*12;
    g('tr-res').innerHTML=
      `<div class="res"><span>Drainage path H<sub>dr</sub></span><b>${Hdr.toFixed(2)} m</b></div>`+
      `<div class="res"><span>Time factor T<sub>v</sub></span><b>${Tv.toFixed(4)}</b></div>`+
      `<div class="verdict v-pass"><span>Time to U = ${U}%</span><b>${t.toFixed(2)} yr (${months.toFixed(1)} mo)</b></div>`+
      `<div class="res"><span>Settlement at U = ${U}%</span><b>${(Sc*U/100).toFixed(1)} mm</b></div>`+
      `<div class="res"><span>Remaining</span><b>${(Sc*(100-U)/100).toFixed(1)} mm</b></div>`;

    // settlement-vs-time curve
    const W=300,Hh=165,x0=40,y0=132,xr=245,yr=100;
    const tmax=TvOf(99)*Hdr*Hdr/cv;
    const PX=tt=>x0+(tt/tmax)*xr, PY=u=>y0-(u/100)*yr;
    let d='';
    for(let u=1;u<=99;u++){
      const tt=TvOf(u)*Hdr*Hdr/cv;
      d+=(u===1?'M ':' L ')+PX(tt).toFixed(1)+' '+PY(u).toFixed(1);
    }
    g('tr-fig').innerHTML=`
    <svg viewBox="0 0 ${W} ${Hh}" style="width:100%;height:auto">
      <line x1="${x0}" y1="${y0-yr-6}" x2="${x0}" y2="${y0}" stroke="var(--bdr2)"/>
      <line x1="${x0}" y1="${y0}" x2="${x0+xr+6}" y2="${y0}" stroke="var(--bdr2)"/>
      <path d="${d}" fill="none" stroke="var(--teal)" stroke-width="2"/>
      <line x1="${x0}" y1="${PY(U).toFixed(1)}" x2="${PX(t).toFixed(1)}" y2="${PY(U).toFixed(1)}" stroke="var(--amb)" stroke-width=".8" stroke-dasharray="3,2"/>
      <line x1="${PX(t).toFixed(1)}" y1="${PY(U).toFixed(1)}" x2="${PX(t).toFixed(1)}" y2="${y0}" stroke="var(--amb)" stroke-width=".8" stroke-dasharray="3,2"/>
      <circle cx="${PX(t).toFixed(1)}" cy="${PY(U).toFixed(1)}" r="3.5" fill="var(--amb)"/>
      <text x="${x0-4}" y="${PY(U).toFixed(1)}" font-size="8" fill="var(--amb)" text-anchor="end">${U}%</text>
      <text x="${PX(t).toFixed(1)}" y="${y0+11}" font-size="8" fill="var(--amb)" text-anchor="middle">${t.toFixed(2)} yr</text>
      <text x="18" y="${y0-yr/2}" font-size="8.5" fill="var(--txt2)" transform="rotate(-90 18 ${y0-yr/2})" text-anchor="middle">U (%)</text>
      <text x="${x0+xr/2}" y="${Hh-3}" font-size="8.5" fill="var(--txt2)" text-anchor="middle">time (years)</text>
    </svg>`;
  }
  ['tr-h','tr-drain','tr-cv','tr-sc','tr-u'].forEach(id=>g(id).addEventListener('input',timeRate));
  timeRate();

  document.querySelectorAll('.quiz .q').forEach(q=>{
    const btns=q.querySelectorAll('button');
    btns.forEach(btn=>btn.addEventListener('click',()=>{
      if(q.classList.contains('answered'))return;
      q.classList.add('answered');
      btns.forEach(b=>{ if(b.dataset.v===q.dataset.a)b.classList.add('correct'); else if(b===btn)b.classList.add('wrong'); });
      const a=document.querySelectorAll('.quiz .q.answered').length;
      const r=document.querySelectorAll('.quiz .q.answered button.correct').length;
      g('quiz-score').textContent=r+' / '+a+' answered correctly so far';
    }));
  });
})();
</script>

</Base>
